|term[epistemic-bound]
  :status settled
  :subject-field addressing
  :layer framing-vocabulary
  :gloss How many the actor believes exist; divergence is dialogue, not failure — and recorded bounds are free calibration.
  :dual-of @operational-bound
  |designation epistemic-bound
    :status preferred
    :channel prose
  |definition
    :defined-by @def-cardinality-and-resolution
    :anchor double-bound
    :projection paraphrase
    The epistemic bound: how many the actor believes exist — "I expect no more than three, or I've grossly misunderstood the data." Divergence is information, ideally a dialogue, never a binary error.
